>>>>> On Fri, 21 May 1993 10:27:53 GMT, dnh@mfltd.co.uk (Des Herriott) said:

Des> Again, no.  You *need* a named weapon to finish the game.

The weapon suggestions should be read together.  You will get a named
weapon in Gehennom, and the chrysknife should be able to get you
there.

Per> - Make it impossible to wish for named weapons.

Per> - Make it impossible to get a named weapon from the Gods.

Per> - Give the priest in Gehennom a named weapon, so the player have one
Per> in Hell.

Per> - A chrysknife should be significantly better than all other non-named
Per> weapons.

The idea is that a chrysknife (or another good weapon) should be
enough to get you to Gehennom.  You should be able to get named
weapons by solving miniquests or killing unique monsters later in the
game.  Actually, I would like to see a miniquest associated with each
unique weapon.

Per> - Remove wands of wishing from the game.  Replace the wand with a
Per> magic lamp in the castle level. 

Des> I disagree here.  Sure, it's possible to get 8 or 9 wishes in a game,
Des> but it doesn't happen often.  And you need that WoW in the castle to
Des> get those items you simply haven't been able to find, like blessed 
Des> tinning kits etc.

The wand of wishing at the castle gives you at least 5 wishes.  If it
is replaced with a blessed magic lamp, you are still guaranteed one
wish, plus wishes from other magic lamps you find, or wishes you can
wrest out of smoky portions, fountains and thrones.
  
BTW, it _is_ possible to complete the game without a blessed tinning
kit.



